    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be the serpentine belt? can you explain how that belt actually works and why it would make that kind of noise if it's worn out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a critical component that powers various engine systems, such as the alternator, air conditioning compressor, and power steering pump. It wraps around multiple pulleys, transmitting rotational motion and voltage to these systems. A worn-out serpentine belt can cause a squealing or squeaking noise, usually during acceleration, due to the belt's surface becoming rough and teeth chattering against the pulleys as they try to maintain their mechanical advantage. This can be an indication that the belt is worn, stretched, or cracked, requiring replacement.",
